…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŞSpeak not evil one of another, brethren. He that speaketh evil of his brother, and judgeth his brother, speaketh evil of the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judge the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]There is one lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy: who art thou that judgest another?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒGo to now, ye that say, To day or to morrow we will go into such a city, and continue there a year, and buy and sell, and get gain:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—whereas ye know not what shall be on the morrow. For what is your life? It is even a vapour, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPFor that ye ought to say, If the Lord will, we shall live, and do this, or that.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙABut now ye rejoice in your boastings: all such rejoicing is evil.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMTherefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin.¦layout ªlast_verse